scripts/adsorbml/
-----------------

The three AdsorbML pipeline scripts

    1-relax_uma_omat.py
    2-run_adsorbml.py
    3-extract_rank.py

were originally written by **Michal Skaličan** (github.com/skalican19) as part
of the repository

    https://github.com/misohu/mo-h-adsorption-gpaw

maintained by **Michal Hucko** (github.com/misohu), and are included here in
modified form. Each file carries an ATTRIBUTION block in its header stating
what was changed relative to the original. `3-extract_rank.py` is included
unmodified.

**Licensing status.** The upstream repository does not currently carry a
licence file, so the terms under which these three files may be redistributed
are not formally established. They are included here for reproducibility of the
computational pipeline described in this repository, with attribution, pending
clarification from the upstream authors. If either author asks for them to be
removed or relicensed, that will be done.

The MIT License in LICENSE therefore applies to the original work in this
repository — everything outside `scripts/adsorbml/` — and not to the three
files listed above.

Derived material
----------------

`scripts/gpaw_h_adsorption.py` and `scripts/generate_structures.py` began as
files from the same upstream repository, authored by Michal Hucko, and have
since been substantially rewritten here: the seven bulk crystal-structure
generators were rebuilt against published crystallographic data, a
stacking-fault guard was added to the slab builder, and the DFT driver gained
restartable relaxation, provenance columns and a consistent H₂ reference. The
crystal-structure corrections are being offered back upstream as a pull
request.

Everything under `hpc/`, `validation/`, `analysis/` and `scripts/`
(`generate_campaign_set.py`, `campaign_stage3_rank.py`) is original work.
